FIX Latest
----------

upstream/OrchestraFIXLatest.xml is FIX Latest at extension pack 312, the
application layer of the FIX protocol, as the FIX Trading Community publishes
it in https://github.com/FIXTradingCommunity/orchestrations. It is copied
unchanged from commit cd24169a2abd8daba7c360987c7a46ca11873a12, and
scripts/upstream_pins.tsv pins it by its git object hash. upstream/LICENSE is
that repository's licence, the Apache License, Version 2.0, whose README
states:

  (c) Copyright 2017-2026 FIX Protocol Limited

  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License"); you may
  not use this file except in compliance with the License.

The file's own metadata carries another rights line: "Copyright (c) FIX
Protocol Ltd. All Rights Reserved." This project reads the repository's
Apache License grant as the terms the file is shared under. It keeps the file
whole and unchanged, rights line included, and takes the narrower course with
everything it derives from the file:

- src/fix_protocol/data/ restates the file's identifiers, names, numbers,
  codes, structure and pedigree as records. Systems that speak FIX must use
  these as FIX writes them.
- It leaves out the text of every documentation element, FIX's descriptions
  of its elements, 29,430 in this edition. Nothing generated from the
  catalogue carries that text, and tests/test_own_words.py checks it.
- The schema's titles and descriptions, the docs and the knowledge bundle are
  this project's own words, written from what each element does. The same
  test refuses any run of four words they share with FIX's descriptions.

This project claims no right in FIX's material. The Apache License that
covers this repository grants rights in this project's own code, schema and
words. FIX's material in upstream/ and in the records stays under the FIX
Trading Community's terms.

The FIX Trading Community's website, https://www.fixtrading.org/, publishes the
FIX specification under its own terms of use. This repository takes nothing
from it: no text, no table and no download.

The names FIX and FIX Trading Community belong to FIX Protocol Ltd. They are
used here only to name the standard.

